ntStyling"><p>This seems useful and sensible, thanks!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>asking whether the new task is something you want to do more than the ol=
d task</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why not just say "whether the new task is a better thing to do than the =
old task"? Like, there's the rule to start your day with whatever has the b=
iggest "ugh field", i.e. whatever is most painful. I get that you're using =
"want to do more than" broadly, but still, it carries the wrong connotation=
 for me. :-)</p>
